@startuml AD_Cube_DrillDown_Workflow
!theme cerulean-outline
title Cube Insights Drill-Down Workflow
footer AdventureWorks Sales BI Platform

|#e8f0fe|User (Browser)|
|#e8f4e8|React Frontend|
|#fff3e0|ASP.NET Core Backend (OlapService)|
|#fce4ec|SSAS Cube (MDX)|

|User (Browser)|
start
:Navigate to **/cube-insights**\n(Cube Insights page);

|React Frontend|
:useEffect triggers\n**loadFilters()**;

:GET /api/cubeinsights/filters;

|ASP.NET Core Backend (OlapService)|
:Execute MDX to fetch\navailable Years and Territories\nfrom [Order Date] and\n[Sales Territory] dimensions;

|React Frontend|
:Populate Year and Territory\ndropdown filters;

|User (Browser)|
:Select **Year** filter\n(e.g. "2013")\nand **Territory** filter\n(e.g. "North America");

|React Frontend|
:All drill states reset to null\n(drillCategory, drillMonth,\ndrillSubcategory, etc.);

:useEffect triggers **loadData()**;

:=== Overview Tab (7 Parallel API Calls) ===;

fork
  :getKpis(params);
fork again
  :getProfitAnalysis(params);
fork again
  :getSalesTrend(params);
fork again
  :getTopProducts(params);
fork again
  :getTerritorySales(params);
fork again
  :getFreightAnalysis(params);
fork again
  :getTargetStatus(params);
end fork

:All calls via\n**Promise.allSettled()**\n-- partial failures tolerated;

|ASP.NET Core Backend (OlapService)|
:OlapService executes MDX queries\nagainst SSAS cube\n[Adventure Works DW2019];

|SSAS Cube (MDX)|
:Return KPIs:\nGross Profit Margin, AOV,\nDiscount Ratio, Effective Tax Rate;

:Return charts:\nSales & Profit Trend (monthly),\nProfitability by Category,\nTop 10 Subcategories,\nTerritory Sales, Freight,\nTarget Status;

|React Frontend|
:Render 4 KPI cards\n+ 4 charts on Overview tab;

note right
  Charts are interactive:
  clicking a data point
  triggers drill-down.
end note

|User (Browser)|
:=== Trend Drill-Down ===\nClick a **month** on the\nSales & Profit Trend chart;

|React Frontend|
:handleTrendClick()\nsets **drillMonth** = clicked month\n(e.g. "2013-06");

:Reload with trendParams\n{ ...params, month: "2013-06" };

|ASP.NET Core Backend (OlapService)|
:MDX uses FILTER on\n[Order Date].[Date].MEMBERS\nfor the selected month;

:Return **daily** sales data\ninstead of monthly;

|React Frontend|
:Chart title changes to\n"Daily Sales & Profit (2013-06)";

:Show "Roll up" button;

|User (Browser)|
:Click **"Roll up"** button;

|React Frontend|
:setDrillMonth(null);
:Reloads with monthly view;

|User (Browser)|
:=== Category Drill-Down ===\n(Category -> Subcategory)\nClick a **category** on the\nProfitability by Category chart;

|React Frontend|
:handleCategoryClick()\nsets **drillCategory** = clicked\n(e.g. "Bikes");

:Reload with profitParams\n{ ...params, category: "Bikes" };

|ASP.NET Core Backend (OlapService)|
:MDX drills into subcategories\nunder the selected category;

:Return profitability data\nfor subcategories\n(e.g. Mountain Bikes, Road Bikes);

|React Frontend|
:Chart title changes to\n"Profitability (Bikes)"\nwith Roll up button;

|User (Browser)|
:=== Product Drill-Down ===\n(Subcategory -> Product)\nClick a **subcategory** on the\nTop Products chart;

|React Frontend|
:handleProductClick()\nsets **drillSubcategory** = clicked\n(e.g. "Mountain Bikes");

:Reload with productParams\n{ ...params, subcategory:\n"Mountain Bikes" };

|ASP.NET Core Backend (OlapService)|
:MDX drills into individual\nproducts within subcategory;

:Return Top 10 Products\nwith Sales and Profit;

|React Frontend|
:Chart title changes to\n"Top 10 Products (Mountain Bikes)"\nwith Roll up button;

|User (Browser)|
:=== Territory Drill-Down ===\n(Group -> Country -> Region)\nClick a **territory group** on\nthe map (e.g. "North America");

|React Frontend|
:handleMapClick()\nsets **drillTerritoryGroup**\n= "North America";

:Reload with territoryParams\n{ ...params, territoryGroup:\n"North America" };

|ASP.NET Core Backend (OlapService)|
:MDX drills from Groups\nto Countries within\nNorth America;

|React Frontend|
:Map re-centers, shows\ncountry-level bubbles\n(US, Canada)\nwith Roll up button;

|User (Browser)|
:Click a **country**\n(e.g. "United States");

|React Frontend|
:handleMapClick()\nsets **drillTerritoryCountry**\n= "United States";

:Reload with territoryParams\n{ ...params,\n  territoryGroup: "North America",\n  territoryCountry: "United States" };

|ASP.NET Core Backend (OlapService)|
:MDX drills from Country\nto Regions within US\n(Southwest, Northwest, etc.);

|React Frontend|
:Map re-centers, shows\nregion-level bubbles;

:Title: "Regions in United States"\nwith Roll up button;

|User (Browser)|
:Click "Roll up" to go back\nto Country or Group level;

|React Frontend|
:If drillTerritoryCountry set:\nclear it (go to country level)\nElse: clear drillTerritoryGroup\n(go to global level);

note right
  All drill patterns follow
  the same approach:
  1. Click sets drill state
  2. useEffect triggers loadData()
  3. Backend applies filters
  4. "Roll up" clears drill state
end note

:=== Additional Tab Drill-Downs ===;

note left
  **Tab 1 - Product Insights:**
  - Cost: Category -> Subcategory -> Product
  - Discount: Category -> Subcategory

  **Tab 4 - Promotions:**
  - Discount Trend: Monthly -> Daily

  **Tab 5 - Fulfillment:**
  - Shipping Volume: Monthly -> Daily
  - Freight: Group -> Country -> Region
end note

stop
@enduml
